      "writtenOn": "2022-09-02T22:20:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think casting just hides the underlying issue. For example, if `fgr` was `UINT32_MAX` and `template_newly_enrolled` was `-1`, the comparison would be true, which is probably not what we want since `template_newly_enrolled` being set to `-1` is supposed to be `FP_NO_SUCH_TEMPLATE`.\n\nWe can\u0027t actually hit this case since we have an earlier check where we return if `fgr \u003e\u003d FP_MAX_FINGER_COUNT`, but like you mentioned in the other comment, it\u0027s weird that we have all these different types for the same thing.\n\nHow about I cast it in this CL (so that we can land the [C++ changes](https://crrev.com/c/3551682)) and then rework the types in a followup commit?",
